ost up to a massive 5  gigahertz which we think is totally  worth it for anyone who can actually use  those extra cores like for raw video  editing now instead of doing that you  can pay just $100 more for the $2,800  model which comes with a slightly slower  but still 8 core processor the faster  560 X graphics chip in twice the storage  space which  think is worth every penny to be  completely honest we don't think there's  gonna be much of a performance  difference between both of those eight  core processors so just going for the  twenty eight hundred dollar model is the  best value we also highly recommend  upgrading to the Vega 20 graphics chip  if you're doing heavy graphics work or  gaming you can watch this video above to  find out why it's well worth the price  now you might be wondering why the  13-inch MacBook Pro is still stuck on  Intel's 8th gen processor instead of  moving on to nine Chen well taking a  look at Intel's 9 Chen product page it  seems as though none of those processors  come with their premium until iris +  graphics which is a must for 13-inch  models since they lack dedicated  graphics chips other than the processor  and keyboard upgrades literally nothing  else has changed which is the most  disappointing part everyone's been  waiting for a complete redesign with  thinner bezels and we unfortunately have  to wait even longer and if Apple was  planning a redesign for sometime this  year they wouldn't have upgraded the  MacBook Pro right now so it seems like  we're going to be waiting until next  year for a redesign and there's still no  word on the rumored 16 inch MacBook Pro  so there's a chance that that model will  include the new redesign and will come  next year we think it makes more sense  for Apple to redesign the iMac first  starting with the iMac Pro potentially  this year and then redesign the MacBook  Pro afterward one thing that's really  disappointing is that Apple's based  13-inch MacBook Pro for $1,300 is still  a 2017 